 5. ⚡ Fetterman&#x27;s surprise convention cameo 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sen. John Fetterman (D-Pa.) introduces Sen. Dave McCormick (R-Pa.) in a video at the Republican convention last night. Photo: Kevin Dietsch/Getty Images Sen. John Fetterman (D-Pa.) made a bombshell appearance last night at the GOP convention in a video praising President Trump and Republican Sen. Dave McCormick for helping America's steel industry, Axios' Alex Isenstadt and Holly Otterbein write from Dallas. 

 Why it matters: Fetterman's stunning turn — a Democratic senator in a supporting role at the GOP's showcase campaign event — marks a dramatic escalation in his growing estrangement from his party. For Democrats, the cameo supercharges questions about whether Fetterman will ultimately leave the Democratic Party before he's up for reelection in 2028. 

 McCormick has courted Fetterman for months. Share this story ... Watch the video . 

 
 
