 6. 🦾 AI fuels small-business boom 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Gusto. Chart: Matt Phillips/Axios Very small businesses that adopt AI actually wind up growing their employee ranks faster compared with those that haven't started using the technology, Axios' Emily Peck writes from a new report by payroll platform Gusto. 

 Overall, small businesses that use AI grew headcount 5% more than non-AI users, on average, in the first year of AI use. 🧮 By the numbers: The effect was strongest for the smallest companies. Businesses with fewer than 10 employees grew their teams by an average of 10% one year after adopting AI, compared with comparable businesses that didn't adopt it.

 Businesses with 10 or more employees didn't see a headcount change. Share this story . 

 
 
