 7. 🕊️ Advice that bolstered Erika Kirk 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A Charlie Kirk shirt for sale at the Republican convention in Dallas yesterday. Photo: Julia Demaree Nikhinson/AP Ahead of today's first anniversary of the assassination of Charlie Kirk, his widow Erika Kirk writes in the N.Y. Times that she's leaned on one piece of advice every day: "Just get through the next 15 minutes."

 That line, from Second Lady Usha Vance, came the day after Kirk was shot and killed. Vance likened getting through it to a bumpy flight: "You know when you're on an airplane with your kids, and you're going to land in 15 minutes, but the kids are going crazy, screaming, throwing things, and then the plane lands, and the kids relax, and everything is fine again? That's how it will be."

